{
  "why": "The ICT Adventure set (original/grade-9/ict-adventure.html) carries Sinhala for its lesson titles and its quiz questions, but not for game names, descriptions, quiz options, sort items, bin labels or memory pairs, so extract.mjs leaves 348 strings at si: null. This file is that Sinhala, drafted 2026-09-20 against the NIE Sinhala-medium terms in content/pages/word-bank.md and against the wording already used in content/grade-9.sinhala.json, so a term cannot read one way in a lesson and another way in a bonus game. Keyed by the English string, per game id; a key that no longer matches fails loudly. Every game it touches is marked siDraft: true until Ishini reviews it.",
  "draft": true,

  "notes": {
    "kept in english on purpose": "Product and standard names (VGA, HDMI, RJ45, USB, RAM, CPU, Wi-Fi, micro:bit, Arduino, Raspberry Pi, Intel i5, ATMEGA328p, ARM Cortex, AMD Ryzen), spreadsheet function names and operators (SUM, AVERAGE, MAX, MIN, =, + - * /), cell addresses (D5, 5D) and bare numbers. A Sinhala-medium student writes these in English too, and translating them would make the answer wrong.",
    "acronym questions": "n2 asks what NIC stands for and n3 asks what CLI stands for. All four options in each are English expansions of the acronym, so translating any of them would destroy the question. They stay English.",
    "bins that already carried sinhala": "n1 and so2 had the Sinhala inside the English bin label, as 'Wired (රැහැන් සහිත)'. The Sinhala side is just the Sinhala, with no bracket."
  },

